  <dimension1_explanation>The AI was working on the correct problem (determining W(n,k) for each pair) and even reached a correct conclusion for one case (W(2,2)=0, the k=n case). However, it missed the crucial structural turning point that the game is winnable if and only if k<n, instead attempting exhaustive case-by-case game-tree analysis. It also incorrectly concluded W(3,2)=0 (which should be 1 since 2<3), and ran out of tokens while still analyzing the k=3,n=3 case without ever identifying the general pattern.</dimension1_explanation>
